BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (The rate engine is where operators make or lose the deal. ClaimDOC prices every facility claim two ways,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (Medicare plus a 25 percent markup and the hospital's own self-reported cost plus a 20 percent markup, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (pays whichever is higher; the cost figure comes from the cost-of-services report every Medicare hospital) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (must file with CMS, which Arif argues is fully loaded because hospitals use it to set their own government) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (reimbursement [mPaz9R2yMrs @ 00:24:54]. The math runs line by line, so the plan can defend every) Tj ET
