BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (broker touted on LinkedIn would scare even Arif [A__ZFq9k8Ds @ 00:48:56]. Kupa's worked example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (shows where the spread lives: a $10,000 billed procedure with a 62.5 percent carrier discount pays $3,750,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (roughly 250 percent of Medicare; Medicare itself pays $1,500; an RBP plan at 150 percent pays $2,250, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (effective 77.5 percent discount [vCzjI43ZWVI @ 00:01:46]. Deihl gives the carrier comparison operators) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (quote against, with insurers averaging about 140 percent of Medicare for hospital services and 120 to 125) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (percent for physician services, higher or lower depending on the carrier [FPcS3pupwwA @ 00:00:41].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (Access is engineered before the first claim drops. ClaimDOC's Pave the Way program pulls the consultant's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (top utilization report, lets members nominate their own doctors during open enrollment and all year, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (calls each office with a fixed script: here is how we pay, how fast we pay, the payer ID, what the card looks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (like, and will you keep charging the $25 copay; that outreach lands about a 95 percent physician acceptance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (rate [mPaz9R2yMrs @ 00:12:17]. Facility care is left to flow through normal pre-certification: Arif estimates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (roughly 85 percent of outpatient procedures clear with no friction, eight or nine of every ten flagged cases) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (settle through a ten-person provider relations team run by a former hospital executive, leaving one or two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (percent that need a delay or a redirect to another facility [mPaz9R2yMrs @ 00:21:38]. In markets locked by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (one dominant system, the plan B is contracting freestanding ambulatory surgery centers, while ERs stay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (covered because the Consolidated Appropriations Act bars them from balance billing the member) Tj ET
